## **Token & Credit Usage Comparison**

---

### **1. SINGLE AGENT SYSTEM**

```
Setup: One AI handles everything
```

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Tokens per request** | High (context grows) |
| **Credits per request** | High (full capability loaded) |
| **Efficiency** | Low |
| **Why** | Agent carries all knowledge, gets confused |

**Example:**
```
Customer: "I need a refund"
↓
Single Agent loads: Support + Sales + Tech + Billing knowledge
↓
Tokens: 4,000 (carrying unnecessary context)
Credits: $0.04 per request
Result: Slow, expensive, often wrong department
```

---

### **2. NORMAL MULTI-AGENT (Flat Structure)**

```
Setup: Multiple agents, no coordination
```

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Tokens per request** | Medium (duplicated work) |
| **Credits per request** | Medium (multiple calls) |
| **Efficiency** | Medium |
| **Why** | Agents consult each other blindly |

**Example:**
```
Customer: "Billing issue"
↓
Router Agent → Billing Agent → Support Agent → Escalation Agent
↓
4 separate API calls
Tokens: 1,500 × 4 = 6,000 total
Credits: $0.06 per request
Result: Redundant processing, higher cost
```

---

### **3. HIERARCHICAL SYSTEM (Kaytx Structure)**

```
Setup: Layered with smart routing
```

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Tokens per request** | Low (only relevant context) |
| **Credits per request** | Low (targeted agents) |
| **Efficiency** | High |
| **Why** | Right agent, right knowledge, right time |

**Example:**
```
Customer: "Billing issue"
↓
Classifier (lightweight, 100 tokens) → CX Agent (billing specialist)
↓
Tokens: 100 (classifier) + 800 (specialist) = 900 total
Credits: $0.009 per request
Result: Fast, cheap, accurate
```

